WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Welcome back to SpaceX Daily, episode 34.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.320
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.380
Today is July 16th, 2026.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.800
Here's what's happening at SpaceX today.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.780
Closing the Flight 12 MISHAP probe removes the last regulatory hold

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.260
on Starship's engine-relight demonstration

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.120
that directly gates Artemis III lander timelines.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.320
Remember, we covered the Starship Flight Test campaign yesterday.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.840
This closure moves the refueling timeline forward

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.220
by removing the final external constraint.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.960
The Federal Aviation Administration has formally closed its investigation

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.880
into the Flight 12 anomaly.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.020
The agency released the vehicle and booster

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.500
for the next test campaign without additional corrective actions.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.960
This decision removes the final external constraint

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.180
on the engine-relight sequence planned for Flight 13.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.660
The re-light demonstration remains the critical gate

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.640
for proving orbital refueling capability ahead of Artemis III.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.200
The next static-fire window at Starbase will confirm

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.960
Raptor ignition reliability under the updated

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.680
propellant conditioning procedures.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.200
The closure follows detailed review of telemetry

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.220
from the prior Flight's performance data

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.340
with no new hardware modifications mandated.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.120
With the regulatory path now open,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.580
the real engineering challenge is the fluid dynamics problem

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.560
the re-light itself must solve.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.820
The engine-relight sequence planned for Starship Flight 13

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.820
must solve a fundamental fluid dynamics problem

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.660
of restarting a cryogenic Raptor in the vacuum of space

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.420
after the vehicle has hosted for tens of minutes.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.660
In microgravity, the remaining liquid oxygen

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.120
and methane stratify inside the tanks,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.780
leaving vapor pockets at the feed lines.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.040
Without active settling thrust or a dedicated

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.520
eulage motor, the turbo pumps risk ingesting gas

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.320
and cavitating on ignition.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.220
SpaceX's approach uses a short RCS burn

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.580
to settle the propellants,

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.520
followed by a carefully timed helium purge

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.080
that clears the lines before the igniter fires.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.100
The energy cost of that settling burn directly reduces

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.880
the payload margin available for the first orbital

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.220
refueling demonstration.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.960
If the re-light succeeds,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.100
the same settling technique becomes the baseline

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.120
for every subsequent tanker flight,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.980
collapsing the propellant transfer timeline from days to hours.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.220
The raw propellants themselves are cheap,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.420
yet the entire mission architecture hinges on whether

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.420
a few kilograms of helium and RCS impulse

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.680
can guarantee liquid at the pump inlet.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.860
A single-failed re-light forces either a heavier settling system

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.960
or a redesign of the tank geometry,

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.880
both of which multiply the per-flight cost

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.700
far beyond the price of the fuel.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.720
Success on flight 13 would validate the settling sequence

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.460
under real orbital conditions

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.380
and directly inform the refueling demonstrations

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.060
required for Artemis III.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.160
SpaceX has registered the name StarMind

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.740
for its planned constellation of orbital AI

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.920
inference satellites.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.180
The architecture pairs starlink laser links

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.740
with onboard accelerators to deliver low latency compute

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.140
to terrestrial users.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.860
Early filings indicate the first demonstration nodes

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.860
will ride on starship once refueling is proven.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.620
The program directly extends the same

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.280
inter-satellite networking already flying on the starlink fleet.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.320
Initial nodes will test inference workloads

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.460
routed through the existing laser mesh.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.800
This naming formalizes the orbital compute thread

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.860
within the broader starlink expansion.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.660
The V5 user terminal introduces a smaller phased array aperture

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.060
and integrated laser link transceiver

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.240
that raises downlink capacity while cutting power draw

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.100
by roughly 15%.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.440
Production units are already shipping to select maritime

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.980
and aviation customers for field validation.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.620
The design change supports the direct to cell waveform

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.880
without requiring a separate modem.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.780
Next milestone is regulatory approval

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.500
for the V5 terminal in additional countries.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.820
The terminal maintains compatibility

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.580
with existing starlink ground infrastructure.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.200
Field test will measure link stability

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.160
under motion and weather conditions

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.220
typical for those customer segments.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.900
The Air Force has begun installing

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.700
star shield flat panel antennas on KC 135 tankers

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:23.800
to provide resilient,

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.780
beyond line-of-site communications

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.440
during refueling operations.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.100
Each aircraft receives two terminals

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.920
that maintain links through the star shield constellation

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:36.180
even when traditional UHF SATCOM is jammed.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.800
The retrofit uses existing fuselage hardpoints

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.220
and adds minimal drag.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.760
Operational testing is scheduled for later this quarter.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.100
The antennas leverage the same phased array technology

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.660
already proven on starlink platforms.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.840
This integration extends star shields role

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.000
in national security communications

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.680
without requiring new airframe modifications.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.420
Regulatory filing show SpaceX has completed

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:05.020
the final spectrum coordination steps required

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.260
for starlink service in the Kurdistan region of Iraq.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.060
Ground stations are already under construction near Erbil.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.920
Service launch is expected within 90 days

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.460
once the final operating license is issued.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.440
The rollout adds another high-demand market

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.640
to the direct-to-sell expansion timeline.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.800
Coordination covered both Q and K-A band allocations

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.920
for the regional beams.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.260
Local partners are preparing distribution channels

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.960
ahead of commercial availability.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.020
Amazon has received regulatory clearance

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.180
to begin beta service for its project

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.580
Kewis constellation in South Africa.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.640
Starlink's own license application remains

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.600
under review by the same authority.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.200
The parallel rollout gives regulators

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.200
a direct comparison of two LEO systems

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.320
in the same market.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.440
Starlink's license decision is expected before year end.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.080
Both operators have proposed

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.800
similar ground segment architectures for the region.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.960
The outcome will set precedent

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.100
for additional African market entries.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.060
A small fire was reported

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.440
at the propellant gasification test stand

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.260
on the star-based production site.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.340
Local fire crews responded

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.640
and contained the incident with no injuries.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.340
The stand supports Raptor engine pre-burner testing

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.060
ahead of the next flight campaign.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.060
Operations at adjacent pads continued uninterrupted.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.680
The event occurred during routine conditioning

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.360
of cryogenic propellants.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.220
Investigation into the cause is underway

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.960
but has not altered the overall test schedule.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:38.300
Observers on X are sharing high-resolution photos

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.160
of the ship 39 heat shield tile layout

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.720
taken during recent stacking operations at starbase.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.800
The pattern shows that denser tile arrangement

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.460
near the leeward side compared with flight 12.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.220
Separate posts note that the mechazilla tower arms

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.240
have been fitted with new capture fixtures

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.840
ahead of the upcoming test.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.120
A third thread tracks the first public sighting

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.880
of a V5 starlink terminal installed on a commercial vessel

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.220
in the Gulf of Mexico.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.220
Worth keeping an eye on,

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.780
starlink satellites are now executing nearly one collision

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.000
avoidance maneuver per week on average,

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.540
according to tracking data and regulatory filings.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.420
The rising frequency consumes propellant reserves

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.620
and shortens on orbit lifetime.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:25.920
Continued growth in both the starlink constellation

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.900
and other LEO traffic will increase the maneuver burden

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.440
unless improved coordination

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.180
or debris mitigation rules are adopted.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.940
Resolution depends on either new

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:39.160
international traffic management agreements

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.940
or hardware upgrades that reduce propellant cost per maneuver.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:46.740
On the AI front, SpaceX has formally named

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.520
its planned orbital AI inference constellation StarMind.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.340
Pairing starlink laser links with onboard accelerators

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.620
for low latency terrestrial compute.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.100
The first nodes are slated to ride on starship

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.880
once refueling is demonstrated.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.660
XAI's Colossus II project in Mississippi

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.980
continues to draw scrutiny over air quality permitting

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.560
for its 59 installed gas turbines.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.740
Cursor vulnerability researchers have published additional

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.900
exploit details that remain unpatched seven months

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.440
after initial disclosure.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.220
The StarMind architecture reuses the intersatellite laser network

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.780
already operating on Starlink satellites.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.140
Early demonstration flights will validate power

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.980
and thermal management for the onboard accelerators

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.280
under orbital conditions.

